            "M =  matrix([2,1,-4],[3,2,-7],[15/4,9/4,-8])\n  F 1  ↦  [0,0,1]     target  [0,0,1]     match:  true\n  F 2  ↦  [1,0,1]     target  [1,0,1]     match:  true\n  F 3  ↦  [0,1,1]     target  [0,1,1]     match:  true\n  F 4  ↦  [1/2,3/4,1]     target  [1/2,3/4,1]     match:  true\nfixing E1, E2, E3 requires:  [m23 = 0,m13 = 0,m32 = 0,m12 = 0,m31 = 0,m21 = 0]\nso M is diagonal:  matrix([m11,0,0],[0,m22,0],[0,0,m33])\nM·U =  [m11,m22,m33]   — proportional to (1,1,1) only if m11 = m22 = m33\nhence M is a scalar matrix, i.e. the identity of PGL(3) ∎"
          ]
        }
      ]
