    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### Harmonic conjugates, with straightedge only\n\nGiven collinear $A, B, C$, the harmonic conjugate $D$ — the point with $(A,B;C,D) = -1$ — can be constructed using **no measurement at all**, only lines:\n\n1. Pick any point $P$ off the line, and any point $Q$ on the line $PC$ (with $Q \\ne P, C$).\n2. Let $R = AQ \\cap PB$ and $S = BQ \\cap PA$.\n3. Then $D = RS \\cap AB$.\n\nThe figure $\\{P, Q, R, S\\}$ with its six connecting lines is a **complete quadrangle**, and the construction is the reason harmonic sets are the projective substitute for measurement: a straightedge cannot find a midpoint, but it *can* find a harmonic conjugate.\n\nTwo checks are worth making, and the second is the punchline:\n\n- The result does not depend on the choices of $P$ and $Q$ — otherwise it would not be a construction at all.\n- **When $D$ is the point at infinity, $C$ is the midpoint of $AB$.** Setting $x_4 \\to \\infty$ in the cross-ratio gives $(x_3-x_1)/(x_3-x_2) = -1$, i.e. $x_3 = (x_1+x_2)/2$. So \"midpoint\" is the affine shadow of \"harmonic conjugate of the point at infinity\" — the metric notion recovered from a projective one plus a choice of line at infinity, exactly as 1.05 predicted.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* The complete-quadrangle construction of the harmonic conjugate */\nharmonic_conjugate(A, B, C, P, Q) := block([R, S],\n  R : meet( join(A, Q), join(P, B) ),\n  S : meet( join(B, Q), join(P, A) ),\n  meet( join(R, S), join(A, B) ) )$\n\nembed(p) := [p[1], p[2], 1]$\nchart(v) := if v[3] = 0 then 'at_infinity else ratsimp([v[1]/v[3], v[2]/v[3]])$\n\n/* A, B, C on the x-axis */\nAh : embed([0,0])$  Bh : embed([6,0])$  Ch : embed([2,0])$\n\n/* Two different auxiliary choices — the answer must not depend on them */\nPh1 : embed([1,3])$   Qh1 : meet( join(Ph1,Ch), join(embed([0,5]), embed([9,1])) )$\nPh2 : embed([4,-2])$  Qh2 : meet( join(Ph2,Ch), join(embed([-3,4]), embed([8,7])) )$\n\nD1 : harmonic_conjugate(Ah, Bh, Ch, Ph1, Qh1)$\nD2 : harmonic_conjugate(Ah, Bh, Ch, Ph2, Qh2)$\nprint(\"D from the first choice of (P,Q):  \", chart(D1))$\nprint(\"D from the second choice of (P,Q): \", chart(D2))$\nprint(\"same point? \", same_point(D1, D2), \"  — the construction is well defined\")$\n\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"cross-ratio (A,B;C,D) = \", cr(Ah, Bh, Ch, D1), \"   — harmonic ✓\")$\n\n/* --- The midpoint case: put D at infinity and see where C must be --- */\nprint(\"\")$\nDinf : [1, 0, 0]$                      /* the point at infinity of the x-axis */\nCmid : harmonic_conjugate(Ah, Bh, Dinf, Ph1,\n                          meet( join(Ph1, Dinf), join(embed([0,5]), embed([9,1])) ))$\nprint(\"harmonic conjugate of the point at infinity = \", chart(Cmid))$\nprint(\"midpoint of A=(0,0) and B=(6,0) is (3,0) — so C is the midpoint ✓\")$\nprint(\"cross-ratio (A,B;Cmid,∞) = \", cr(Ah, Bh, Cmid, Dinf))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 17,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "D from the first choice of (P,Q):   [-6,0]\nD from the second choice of (P,Q):  [-6,0]\nsame point?  true   — the construction is well defined\ncross-ratio (A,B;C,D) =  -1    — harmonic ✓\nharmonic conjugate of the point at infinity =  [3,0]\nmidpoint of A=(0,0) and B=(6,0) is (3,0) — so C is the midpoint ✓\ncross-ratio (A,B;Cmid,∞) =  -1"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* --- Perspectivity: projecting one line onto another from a centre --- */\n/* This is what a camera does, and what a painter's perspective construction does. */\nperspect(O, lprime, X) := meet( join(O, X), lprime )$\n\nOc : embed([2, 7])$                 /* centre of projection (the eye) */\nl1 : join(embed([0,0]), embed([1,0]))$        /* the object line, y = 0     */\nl2 : join(embed([0,3]), embed([1,5/2]))$      /* the image line (the canvas) */\n\n/* Four points on the object line, at irregular spacing */\nX : map(lambda([t], embed([t, 0])), [0, 1, 3, 7])$\nY : map(lambda([P], perspect(Oc, l2, P)), X)$\n\nprint(\"object points : \", map(chart, X))$\nprint(\"image points  : \", map(chart, Y))$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"spacings on the object line: \", [1-0, 3-1, 7-3], \"  — unequal\")$\nprint(\"cross-ratio on the object line : \", cr(X[1],X[2],X[3],X[4]))$\nprint(\"cross-ratio on the image line  : \", cr(Y[1],Y[2],Y[3],Y[4]))$\nprint(\"preserved — this is why a photograph determines the proportions\")$\nprint(\"of what it photographs, even though it preserves no distance.\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 18,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "object points :  [[0,0],[1,0],[3,0],[7,0]]\nimage points  :  [[3/4,21/8],[4/3,7/3],[36/13,21/13],[68/9,-(7/9)]]\nspacings on the object line:  [1,2,4]   — unequal\ncross-ratio on the object line :  9/7\ncross-ratio on the image line  :  9/7\npreserved — this is why a photograph determines the proportions\nof what it photographs, even though it preserves no distance."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* Draw the complete quadrangle that constructs D from A, B, C */\nRq : meet( join(Ah, Qh1), join(Ph1, Bh) )$\nSq : meet( join(Bh, Qh1), join(Ph1, Ah) )$\n\naff(V)   := float(chart(V))$\nseg(p,q) := [discrete, [p[1], q[1]], [p[2], q[2]]]$\nmark(ps) := [discrete, map(first, ps), map(second, ps)]$\n\npA : aff(Ah)$  pB : aff(Bh)$  pC : aff(Ch)$  pD : aff(D1)$\npP : aff(Ph1)$ pQ : aff(Qh1)$ pR : aff(Rq)$  pS : aff(Sq)$\nprint(\"P = \", pP, \"  Q = \", pQ)$\nprint(\"R = \", pR, \"  S = \", pS)$\nprint(\"A = \", pA, \"  B = \", pB, \"  C = \", pC, \"  D = \", pD)$\nprint(\"D, R, S collinear? \",\n      is( abs(float(det3(D1, Rq, Sq))) < 1e-9 ), \"  — so the thick line is DRS\")$\n\nplot2d([ seg([-7,0], [7,0]),                         /* the base line AB    */\n         seg(pP,pQ), seg(pA,pQ), seg(pB,pQ),         /* quadrangle edges    */\n         seg(pP,pA), seg(pP,pB),\n         seg(pD,pS),                                  /* the line RS, extended to D */\n         mark([pA,pB,pC,pD]), mark([pP,pQ,pR,pS]) ],\n       [x, -7, 7], [y, -3, 6],\n       [style, [lines,1],[lines,1],[lines,1],[lines,1],[lines,1],[lines,1],\n               [lines,3],[points,4],[points,3]],\n       [legend, false], [same_xy, true],\n       [title, \"complete quadrangle PQRS: D = RS ∩ AB is harmonic to C\"])$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 19,
      "outputs": [
